# Media-resources backend

Sibling repo: `/Users/pawansaxena/playpen/21days-media-resources`  
Source of truth: `api/flask_api_server.py`, `DESIGN.md`  
Base URL: `AppConstants.apiBaseUrl` (`http://127.0.0.1:5005` local, or Cloud Run via `--dart-define=API_BASE_URL=…`)

When changing networking, models, or Live/Resources screens, prefer calling these public APIs — do not invent parallel shapes.

## Public APIs used by the app

| Method | Path | Body / notes |
|--------|------|----------------|
| GET | `/health` | `{ "status": "healthy" }` |
| GET | `/api/live/sessions` | Next/current session; URLs from `config/live_sessions.json` |
| GET | `/api/live/recent` | Latest completed livestream per channel within ~72h (≤1 each) |
| GET | `/api/recordings` | Latest year playlist sliced into sessions (oldest-first) |
| GET | `/api/wisdom/topics` | Static Wisdom tab topics from `config/wisdom_topics.json` |
| GET | `/api/videos/<video_id>/chapters` | Chroma timestamp chapters (empty if not ingested) |
| POST | `/search` | `{ "query": string, "top_k"?: int }` → video timestamp sections |
| POST | `/api/resources/search` | `{ "query": string, "top_k"?: int }` → handouts |

### Live session response (`GET /api/live/sessions`)

YouTube-backed. Prefers an active live stream on configured channels; else the
soonest upcoming within ~72h. `session` may be `null`.

```json
{
  "server_time": "ISO-8601",
  "session": {
    "id": "live_<videoId>|upcoming_<videoId>",
    "status": "live|upcoming",
    "source": "youtube_live|youtube_upcoming",
    "video_id": "…",
    "title": "…",
    "channel_id": "…",
    "channel_title": "…",
    "channel_handle": "@…",
    "starts_at": "ISO-8601|null",
    "ends_at": "ISO-8601|null",
    "youtube_live_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=…",
    "youtube_thumbnail_url": "https://…",
    "zoom_meeting_url": "https://zoom.us/j/…"
  }
}
```

### Recent recordings (`GET /api/live/recent`)

At most one completed livestream per configured channel, ending within
`recent_within_hours` (default 72).

```json
{
  "server_time": "ISO-8601",
  "within_hours": 72,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "ended_<videoId>",
      "status": "ended",
      "source": "youtube_completed",
      "video_id": "…",
      "title": "…",
      "channel_id": "…",
      "channel_title": "…",
      "channel_handle": "@…",
      "starts_at": "ISO-8601|null",
      "ends_at": "ISO-8601|null",
      "published_at": "ISO-8601|null",
      "youtube_watch_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=…",
      "youtube_thumbnail_url": "https://…"
    }
  ]
}
```

Edit channels / Zoom in backend `config/live_sessions.json` — not hardcoded in Flutter.

### Year recordings (`GET /api/recordings`)

Latest `year` in `config/year_playlists.json`. Playlist items are sorted oldest-first
and sliced by each session’s `video_count` (split sessions like 3A+3B share 21).
Session `starts_at` / `ends_at` come from static `start_date` / `end_date` in that
config (YYYY-MM-DD), not from YouTube publish times.

```json
{
  "year": 2026,
  "title": "21 Days 2026",
  "playlist_id": "PLxxxx",
  "sessions": [
    {
      "id": "2026-s1",
      "label": "Session 1",
      "video_count": 21,
      "starts_at": "YYYY-MM-DD",
      "ends_at": "YYYY-MM-DD",
      "videos": [
        {
          "video_id": "…",
          "title": "…",
          "published_at": "ISO-8601",
          "youtube_watch_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=…",
          "youtube_thumbnail_url": "https://…"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Map in `YearRecordings` / `RecordingSession` / `SessionVideo`. Session video tap
opens `VideoPlayerScreen` via `RecordingResult`.

### Wisdom topics (`GET /api/wisdom/topics`)

Shared catalog for web and mobile. Edit `config/wisdom_topics.json` (or
`WISDOM_TOPICS_CONFIG`). Mobile falls back to a bundled copy if the API is down.

```json
{
  "heading": "Meditation wisdom",
  "subtitle": "Foundational Sahaja Yoga topics to deepen your attention.",
  "topics": [
    {
      "id": "origin-of-sahaja-yoga",
      "title": "The origin of Sahaja Yoga",
      "subtitle": "Shri Mataji and the gift of Self-Realization",
      "accent_label": "Origins",
      "body": "…"
    }
  ]
}
```

Map in `WisdomTopic` / `WisdomTopicsResponse`.

### Video chapters (`GET /api/videos/<video_id>/chapters`)

Chroma `timestamp_section` rows for one video, sorted oldest-first. Empty
`chapters` when the video is not ingested (no YouTube call).

```json
{
  "video_id": "…",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "timestamp": "4:12",
      "section_title": "Meditation",
      "start_seconds": 252
    }
  ]
}
```

Map in `VideoChapter`. Player shows title+time rows; tap seeks in-app.

### Search result card (`POST /search` → `results[]`)

Fields: `video_title`, `section_title`, `video_id`, `timestamp`, `summary`, `url`, `chakra`, `quote`, `hashtags`, `published_at`, `confidence`, optional `section_duration_seconds`, `chroma_id`.

### Handout result card (`POST /api/resources/search` → `results[]`)

Fields: `resource_id`, `title`, `description`, `topic`, `tags` (array), `download_url`, `file_type`, `created_at`, `confidence`.

Map these in `RecordingResult` / `HandoutResult` / `LiveSession` / `YearRecordings` — keep snake_case JSON ↔ Dart models in sync.

## Explore tab UI conventions

- Tabs: **Videos** → `/search`, **Handouts** → `/api/resources/search`
- Video card tap → in-app YouTube player at `timestamp` (web may open watch URL)
- After closing the player, that card shows **Find similar clips**
- Similar clips → `POST /api/videos/related` with `{ id: chroma_id }` or `{ video_id, timestamp }`
- Related banner: “Showing more like: …” + **← Back to Search Result**
- Handout card tap → open `download_url` externally
- Respect `GET /api/ui-config` → `enableMoreLikeThis` (default true)
- Match card fields from sibling `ui/search.html`

## Conventions

- No mock search/session paths; fail clearly if the API is unreachable.
- Admin/mutating routes (`/api/*/ingest`, resource PUT) are **not** for the mobile client.
- If the backend contract changes, update `lib/services/*` + models together, and skim sibling `DESIGN.md` / Flask routes before inventing fields.
- For deeper backend edits, open or `@`-mention files under `../21days-media-resources/`.
